---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout section="Grant Types">
  <div class="page-wrap">
    <div class="learn-layout">
      <nav class="toc">
        <div class="toc-label">On this page</div>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#decision">Grant Type Decision Table</a></li>
          <li><a href="#auth-code">Authorization Code Flow</a></li>
          <li><a href="#pkce">PKCE Extension</a></li>
          <li><a href="#client-creds">Client Credentials Flow</a></li>
          <li><a href="#implicit">Implicit Flow (Deprecated)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#device">Device Authorization Flow</a></li>
          <li><a href="#refresh">Refresh Tokens</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>

      <main class="content">
        <header class="page-header">
          <h1>OAuth 2.0 Grant Types</h1>
          <span class="badge badge-intermediate">Intermediate</span>
        </header>

        <section id="decision">
          <h2>Grant Type Decision Table</h2>
          <table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin-bottom:1rem;">
            <thead>
              <tr style="border-bottom:2px solid #ccc; text-align:left;">
                <th>App Type</th>
                <th>Client Type</th>
                <th>Grant Type</th>
                <th>Reason</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
                <td>Server-side web app</td>
                <td>Confidential</td>
                <td>Authorization Code</td>
                <td>Back-channel exchange</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
                <td>SPA (React/Vue)</td>
                <td>Public</td>
                <td>Auth Code + PKCE</td>
                <td>No client secret</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
                <td>Mobile / Native</td>
                <td>Public</td>
                <td>Auth Code + PKCE</td>
                <td>Binary can be decompiled</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
                <td>Microservice/Daemon</td>
                <td>Confidential</td>
                <td>Client Credentials</td>
                <td>No user involved</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
                <td>IoT / Smart TV</td>
                <td>Public</td>
                <td>Device Authorization</td>
                <td>No keyboard</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>(Deprecated)</td>
                <td>-</td>
                <td>Resource Owner Password</td>
                <td>Avoid</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </section>

        <section id="auth-code">
          <h2>Authorization Code Flow</h2>
          <p>Defined in RFC 6749 Section 4.1. This is the most common and secure flow for apps that involve a user.</p>
          
          <div style="margin-top:1rem;">
            <div style="border-left:4px solid #f1c40f; padding-left:1rem; margin-bottom:1rem;">
              <strong>Step 1: Authorization Request (Front Channel)</strong><br>
              <pre><code>GET /authorize?response_type=code
&amp;client_id=s6BhdRkqt3
&amp;state=xyz
&amp;redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fclient%2Eexample%2Ecom%2Fcb</code></pre>
            </div>
            
            <div style="border-left:4px solid #f1c40f; padding-left:1rem; margin-bottom:1rem;">
              <strong>Step 2: Authorization Response (Front Channel)</strong><br>
              <pre><code>HTTP/1.1 302 Found
Location: https://client.example.com/cb?code=SplxlOBeZQQYbYS6WxSbIA
&amp;state=xyz</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div style="border-left:4px solid #2ecc71; padding-left:1rem; margin-bottom:1rem;">
              <strong>Step 3: Token Request (Back Channel)</strong><br>
              <pre><code>POST /token HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Authorization: Basic czZCaGRSa3F0MzpnWDFmQmF0M2JW

grant_type=authorization_code&amp;code=SplxlOBeZQQYbYS6WxSbIA
&amp;redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fclient%2Eexample%2Ecom%2Fcb</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div style="border-left:4px solid #2ecc71; padding-left:1rem; margin-bottom:1rem;">
              <strong>Step 4: Token Response (Back Channel)</strong><br>
              <pre><code>HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json

&#123;
  "access_token":"2YotnFZFEjr1zCsicMWpAA",
  "token_type":"bearer",
  "expires_in":3600,
  "refresh_token":"tGzv3JOkF0XG5Qx2TlKWIA"
&#125;</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="pkce">
          <h2>PKCE Extension (RFC 7636)</h2>
          <p>Proof Key for Code Exchange (PKCE) protects the Authorization Code flow from interception attacks.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Generate a random string called <code>code_verifier</code>.</li>
            <li>Compute the <code>code_challenge</code>: <code>BASE64URL(SHA256(code_verifier))</code>.</li>
            <li>Send the <code>code_challenge</code> and <code>code_challenge_method=S256</code> in the <code>/authorize</code> request.</li>
            <li>Send the original <code>code_verifier</code> in the <code>/token</code> request. The server verifies the hash matches.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section id="client-creds">
          <h2>Client Credentials Flow</h2>
          <p>RFC 6749 Section 4.4. Used for machine-to-machine communication where there is no user context.</p>
          <pre><code>POST /token HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Authorization: Basic czZCaGRSa3F0MzpnWDFmQmF0M2JW

grant_type=client_credentials</code></pre>
        </section>

        <section id="implicit">
          <h2>Implicit Flow (Deprecated)</h2>
          <div class="callout warning">
            <strong>Warning:</strong> Deprecated in OAuth 2.1. Do not use.
          </div>
          <p>The implicit flow (<code>response_type=token</code>) returned tokens directly in the URL fragment. It suffered from token leakage in browser history, lack of CSRF protection, and could not issue refresh tokens.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="device">
          <h2>Device Authorization Flow</h2>
          <p>RFC 8628. For devices without a browser or keyboard (e.g., Smart TVs).</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Device requests a code from the Authorization Server.</li>
            <li>Server returns a <code>user_code</code> and a <code>verification_uri</code>.</li>
            <li>Device displays the URI and code to the user. User completes login on their phone.</li>
            <li>Device polls the token endpoint until the user finishes.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section id="refresh">
          <h2>Refresh Tokens</h2>
          <p>RFC 6749 Section 6. Refresh tokens are used to obtain new access tokens without requiring the user to log in again.</p>
          <table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin-top:1rem;">
            <thead>
              <tr style="border-bottom:2px solid #ccc; text-align:left;">
                <th>Feature</th>
                <th>Access Token</th>
                <th>Refresh Token</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
                <td>Sent to APIs</td>
                <td>Yes</td>
                <td>No (Never)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
                <td>Sent to /token</td>
                <td>No</td>
                <td>Yes</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Lifetime</td>
                <td>Short (e.g., 15 mins)</td>
                <td>Long (e.g., 30 days)</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </section>

        <footer class="page-footer">
          <div class="prev-next">
            <a href={base + '/oauth'}>&larr; Prev: OAuth 2.0</a>
            <a href={base + '/oidc'}>Next: OIDC &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </footer>
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
